---
import { sitePath } from '../data/paths';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import PageLayout from '../components/PageLayout.astro';
import NextStep from '../components/NextStep.astro';
import { ecuImages, ecuCases, ecuSteps, ecuFaq } from '../data/ecu';
import { contact, japaneseEcuSite } from '../data/site';
---
<PageLayout title="ECU Flashing" heading="ECU Flashing & Setup" description="Motorcycle ECU Flashing and setup at eFactory, Suzuka. Explore riding checks, data logging and documented GROM, GSX-R750 and ZX-4R examples. Compatibility is checked individually." intro="Beyond peak power. Work towards engine response that fits the way you ride—using vehicle condition, data and riding feedback to consider throttle opening, drive and deceleration." eyebrow="RIDE. CHECK. REFINE." brandLogo={ecuImages.logo}>
  <figure slot="visual" class="page-photo ecu-rider"><Image src={ecuImages.riding} alt="Etsugo Yanagida riding in motogymkhana, as shown on the Japanese ECU page" width={598} widths={[300,598]} sizes="(max-width: 760px) 90vw, 42vw" format="png" loading="eager" /><figcaption>Check it on the motorcycle. Etsugo Yanagida · Riding photograph</figcaption></figure>
  <div slot="intro-extra" class="inline-actions"><a class="button" href={contact.ecuLine}>Enquire about ECU Flashing <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true"></span></a><p class="price-note">Start by checking the model and specification. Detailed technical consultation is separate and may carry a charge.</p></div>
  <section class="story-split content-section"><div><p class="eyebrow">01 / YOUR RIDING</p><h2>What would you like to change?</h2></div><div><ul class="ecu-concerns"><li>Jerky response as you first open the throttle</li><li>A motorcycle that feels difficult to manage at low speed</li><li>Engine braking that feels too strong</li><li>Checking fuelling after modifications</li><li>Adjusting the response for motogymkhana</li></ul><p>The cause may lie outside the ECU. Vehicle condition is checked before considering what flashing can address.</p></div></section>
  <section class="content-section"><p class="eyebrow">02 / OUR APPROACH</p><h2>Ride it. Feel it. Refine it.</h2><p>Changing ECU data is one step. What matters is how that change connects with the rider’s inputs.</p><div class="note-grid ecu-approach"><article><h3>Share your goals</h3><p>Describe when and how the motorcycle feels different from what you want—for example, initial throttle response or drive at low speed.</p></article><article><h3>Check what can be adjusted</h3><p>Fuel, ignition, engine braking and other controls vary by motorcycle and ECU. Adjustments are considered against the actual specification.</p></article><article><h3>Ride and verify</h3><p>Where needed, measurements and logging support riding checks and rider feedback as the response is refined.</p></article></div><details class="ecu-explainer"><summary>What is “transient response”?</summary><p>It is the engine’s response when your inputs change, such as opening or closing the throttle, rather than only at a steady engine speed. The feeling from input to drive matters alongside maximum power. Measurement and riding-check methods are agreed for the motorcycle and the work.</p></details></section>
  <section class="content-section"><p class="eyebrow">03 / SETTING STORIES</p><h2>Setup, seen through real examples.</h2><p>Each motorcycle and purpose is different. These examples follow the public work records used on the latest Japanese ECU page.</p><div class="ecu-case-grid">{ecuCases.map(item => <article class="ecu-case"><Image src={item.image} alt={item.alt} width={680} widths={[340,680]} sizes="(max-width: 760px) 90vw, 28vw" format="png" loading="lazy" /><div class="ecu-case-copy"><p class="eyebrow">{item.tag}</p><h3>{item.name}</h3><p class="ecu-case-title">{item.title}</p><dl><dt>Purpose</dt><dd>{item.purpose}</dd><dt>Adjustments</dt><dd>{item.adjustment}</dd><dt>What is documented</dt><dd>{item.result}</dd></dl><a href={`${japaneseEcuSite}cases/${item.slug}/`} class="text-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read the case in Japanese <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true"></span></a></div></article>)}</div><p class="price-note">These are records for individual motorcycles and conditions. They do not guarantee a performance improvement or the same result for another vehicle.</p></section>
  <section class="content-section"><p class="eyebrow">04 / HOW IT WORKS</p><h2>From enquiry to explaining the findings.</h2><ol class="process-list">{ecuSteps.map(([title,text],index) => <li><span>{String(index+1).padStart(2,'0')}</span><div><h3>{title}</h3><p>{text}</p></div></li>)}</ol><p class="price-note">Confirm pricing, lead time, further adjustments and on-site arrangements before work begins. These depend on the motorcycle and project.</p></section>
  <section class="content-section"><p class="eyebrow">05 / QUESTIONS</p><h2>Before you arrange ECU work.</h2><div class="faq-list">{ecuFaq.map(([question,answer]) => <details><summary>{question}</summary><p>{answer}</p></details>)}</div><div class="ecu-conditions"><h3>Points to confirm before work</h3><p>Confirm how the original ECU will be handled, the price, and implications for Japanese vehicle inspection, manufacturer warranty and fault risks. ECU Flashing does not guarantee performance, safety or legal compliance.</p></div></section>
  <section class="content-section enquiry-checklist"><div><p class="eyebrow">06 / LET’S TALK</p><h2>How would you like your bike to respond?</h2><p>Enquiry reception and detailed diagnosis or setup consultation are separate. Detailed technical advice may carry a fee; confirm the scope and fees in advance. English-language arrangements also need to be confirmed.</p></div><ul><li>Motorcycle model and model code</li><li>Year, if known</li><li>Modified parts</li><li>Current symptoms</li><li>Desired response and intended use</li></ul></section>
  <NextStep title="Start with your current motorcycle." text="Send your model, specification and concerns using the official ECU LINE account." href={contact.ecuLine} label="ECU enquiry on LINE" />
  <a class="text-link section-link" href={sitePath('/contact/')}>General contact & access <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true"></span></a>
</PageLayout>
